```js
function debounce(fn, delay) {
  let timer;
  return function(...args) {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    timer = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), delay);
  };
}
```
Debouncing delays function execution until a specified idle duration has elapsed since the last event invocation.

```js
function throttle(fn, limit) {
  let inThrottle;
  return function(...args) {
    if (!inThrottle) {
      fn.apply(this, args);
      inThrottle = true;
      setTimeout(() => inThrottle = false, limit);
    }
  };
}
```
Throttling enforces a maximum execution rate, ensuring the function fires at most once per defined time interval.

